 "committedCopy": "The control for same-break-apartments: the same five poses, the same two sides, NO sabotage. PASS --same 1%, exit 0, A/B pixels over 16 luma min 0.000 / median 0.003 / max 0.005 over 5 frames. Both sides took 2 reloads then the APARTMENTS.on poke, symmetrically, and every shot has tilesOk true, so it is clean under the load-asymmetry rule added in the fifth pass. It predates the report.exit field, so its exit 0 is read off an empty verdict.uninterpretable and an empty verdict.same.failing. Absolute paths rewritten; nothing else changed. ||| SIXTH PASS, 2026-09-20 -- RE-MEASURED, NOT RE-SHOT. The two Capitol poses' `wall` and `dome` rectangles were on MapLibre's own fill-extrusions, not on anything we author: `--break slopes` deleted 3,560,273 triangles and every measured number at both poses came back bit-identical. wall and dome are now read off the A-vs-B mask of that run (92-96% of each rectangle is pixels the sabotage changed by more than 3 of 255 on any channel; 86-91% at a threshold of 6), the old rectangles are kept as `downtown`/`flanking` and declared `basemap`, and every kept report was re-measured from its OWN frames with --from against the corrected night-routes.json. No frame in this file was taken again; the frames are byte-for-byte the ones the shoot produced. Capitol numbers before and after are tabulated in docs/night-implementation-plan.md sec W0a. Every shot also gained `frame.bytes`/`frame.sha1`, and `report.exit` now exists in all ten files.",
